-- title:
--   Integrality away from v means r-power denominators
-- statement:
--   Let $a_1,b_1\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the rational quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ which is an order in the sense used here, i.e. $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module. Let $r$ be a prime natural number and let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ whose ideal contains the image of $r$, so that $v$ is the place above $r$. Then for $y\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ the following are equivalent: (i) for every height-one prime $w\neq v$, the element $y\otimes 1$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ lies in [`Submodule.localBox Λ w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), the additive subgroup generated by the tensors $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of the $w$-adic completion of $\mathbb{Q}$; (ii) there is a natural number $K$ with $(r^K)\cdot y\in\Lambda$, the scalar being the rational number $r^K$.
--
--   This is the local–global dictionary for the lattice $\Lambda$ in the form needed away from a single place: the elements of the quaternion algebra that are integral at every finite place other than $v$ are exactly those with denominator a power of $r$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, for instance in the analysis of the coset graph and of the group of units away from $r$ attached to Eichler orders.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_forall_tmul_one_mem_localBox_iff_exists_pow_smul_mem.lean

